<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gedrosia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gedrosia was an ancient region corresponding to present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Balochistan</a>, along the coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-mauryan-war">Treaty of the Indus</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a> ceded Gedrosia, along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arachosia">Arachosia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paropamisadae">Paropamisadae</a>, to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> in exchange for 500 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gedrosia.jpg" alt="Gedrosia" width="320" height="159" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.r ebrahim zadeh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gedrosia-Maka_(Satrapy_of_the_Achaemenid_Empire).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
